  <aside class="rail" data-marble-id="notebook-rail">
    <h1 data-marble-id="notebook-title" data-marble-editable>Week 12: Head Ablations</h1>
    <ol data-marble-id="note-list" id="note-list" class="note-list" data-marble-sortable="notes">
      <li data-marble-id="note-hypothesis" data-folder="Lab" data-pinned="true" data-locked="false" data-updated="2026-11-23T02:20:51.462Z" data-marble-removable>
        <p data-marble-id="note-hypothesis-title" data-marble-editable>Hypothesis &amp; Ablations</p>
        <span data-marble-id="note-hypothesis-snippet" class="snippet">The early-layer heads are doing position, not semantics. Ablate them only after the seed is froz</span>
      </li>
      <li data-marble-id="note-probes" data-folder="Lab" data-pinned="false" data-locked="false" data-updated="2026-11-22T20:20:51.462Z" data-marble-removable>
        <p data-marble-id="note-probes-title" data-marble-editable>Attention Head Probes</p>
        <span data-marble-id="note-probes-snippet" class="snippet">Linear probes on the residual stream, fit per head, scored on the previous-token copy task. A he</span>
      </li>
      <li data-marble-id="note-spike" data-folder="Lab" data-pinned="false" data-locked="false" data-updated="2026-11-23T02:21:05.539Z" data-marble-removable>
        <p data-marble-id="note-spike-title" data-marble-editable>Loss Spike Postmortem</p>
        <span data-marble-id="note-spike-snippet" class="snippet">Step 48,200. Loss 2.1 to 6.4 in forty steps, then a stall. The data order hash did not match the</span>
      </li>
      <li data-marble-id="note-queue" data-folder="Lab" data-pinned="false" data-locked="false" data-updated="2026-11-22T08:20:51.462Z" data-marble-removable>
        <p data-marble-id="note-queue-title" data-marble-editable>Reading Queue</p>
        <span data-marble-id="note-queue-snippet" class="snippet">Olsson et al. (2022): In-context learning and induction heads Elhage et al. (2021): A mathematic</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </aside>
  <div data-marble-id="note-stage" id="note-stage" class="stage">
    <article data-marble-id="pane-note-hypothesis" data-note="note-hypothesis">
      <h2 data-marble-id="pane-note-hypothesis-h" data-marble-editable>Hypothesis &amp; Ablations</h2>
      <div data-marble-id="pane-note-hypothesis-body" class="md-body" data-marble-editable>The early-layer heads are doing position, not semantics. Ablate them only after the seed is frozen, or the loss spike and the ablation get blamed on each other.

- [ ] Freeze seeds before the sweep
- [x] Log the data order hash
- [ ] Write the failed run before the next one</div>
    </article>
    <article data-marble-id="pane-note-probes" data-note="note-probes">
      <h2 data-marble-id="pane-note-probes-h" data-marble-editable>Attention Head Probes</h2>
      <div data-marble-id="pane-note-probes-body" class="md-body" data-marble-editable>Linear probes on the residual stream, fit per head, scored on the previous-token copy task. A head that probes well and ablates clean is a circuit, not a correlation.

### L2H4
Copies the previous token. Ablation raises copy loss by 0.4 without moving the main loss.

### L5H1
Induction head. Probe accuracy 0.91. Leave it in until the name-mover is mapped.</div>
    </article>
    <article data-marble-id="pane-note-spike" data-note="note-spike">
      <h2 data-marble-id="pane-note-spike-h" data-marble-editable>Loss Spike Postmortem</h2>
      <div data-marble-id="pane-note-spike-body" class="md-body" data-marble-editable>Step 48,200. Loss 2.1 to 6.4 in forty steps, then a stall. The data order hash did not match the logged run.

### Timing

Just after the learning-rate decay, on the shard that was reshuffled by hand.

### Root cause

Not the ablation. The spike reproduces with every head intact if the shard hash differs.</div>
    </article>
    <article data-marble-id="pane-note-queue" data-note="note-queue">
      <h2 data-marble-id="pane-note-queue-h" data-marble-editable>Reading Queue</h2>
      <div data-marble-id="pane-note-queue-body" class="md-body" data-marble-editable>1. Olsson et al. (2022): In-context learning and induction heads
2. Elhage et al. (2021): A mathematical framework for transformer circuits
3. Power et al. (2022): Grokking and generalization beyond overfitting</div>
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
